# M44 (Exact) Execution Changes Log — Exact Avatar Silhouette & Data Views

Autonomous sprint following the strict TDD loop per task. This pass refines the
avatar silhouette to its exact intended proportions and re-verifies the
green-stomach, grid and history-data work under a single M44 contract. Tasks 2–4
were first delivered in the earlier M44 sprint (commits on `main`) and are
re-verified here rather than rewritten.

## Task 1: Exact Avatar Silhouette Restoration
- `lib/ui/organisms/body_blueprint/body_segment_geometry.dart`
  - Slimmer limb half-widths (units of figure height): upper arms `0.052→0.042`,
    forearms `0.045→0.034`, thighs `0.075→0.062`, calves `0.058→0.046`.
  - `jointGap` increased `0.016→0.022` for a cleaner, unmistakable elbow/knee
    articulation.
  - `_torso` sides are now cubic Béziers: the upper control flares to the wider
    baseline half-width (rounded shoulder / belly bulge) and the lower control
    returns toward the narrower half-width, producing a smooth continuous waist
    contour. Controls never exceed the wider half-width, so path bounds and all
    hit tests are unchanged.
- `lib/ui/organisms/body_blueprint/body_blueprint_painter.dart` — outline stroke
  `1.6→1.4` for a crisp technical line.
- `test/ui/avatar_silhouette_test.dart` — limb-width envelopes, "slimmer than the
  previous silhouette" contract, joint-gap assertions, and closed-contour checks.
- `test/ui/goldens/body_blueprint_painter.png` regenerated.

